--- !u!114 &359414593
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 359414592}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2a700b90d31390a4da5db3aef9eed1f4, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::LibroTest
  paginaVisual: {fileID: 527430855}
  coloresPagina: []
  textosPaginas:
  - From the starry night sky, on a warm summer's day, A sweet gift fell down, like
    an angel at play. A star-child arriving from a world far apart, Came down just
    to heal a poor mother's sad heart.
  - The little one shone like a treasure of light, The perfect excuse to chase off
    the dark night. Suddenly the universe felt right and so glad, And the weeping
    finally stopped for the dad.
  - The sweet songs of love regained all their gleam, The mother and child ruled
    a castle of dream. But sometimes the queens get too tired to reign, And it's
    hard to carry the weight of the pain.
  - The father of the house went to search for a star, Leaving the mother with a
    sorrow so far. Her pain was an ocean, so deep and so cold, She locked herself
    up, feeling broken and old.
  - Seeking the silence, she closed up her room, Ignoring the wind that brought whispers
    of gloom. Then from the dark sky, with a smile bright and sweet, Another guest
    fell in the meadow to greet.
  - With skin soft as velvet, a stranger from space, Reached our small world in a
    stellar embrace. Two beings from out there, two souls from afar, Met right in
    the yard like a beautiful star.
  - Seeing the stranger, she greeted with grace, "A friend made of gold!" thought
    the mom in her place. They played hide-and-seek by the rose garden wall, Two
    sweet little visitors, having a ball.
  - 'They splashed in the puddles beneath the soft rain, Sharing strawberry ice cream
    again and again. The mother watched softly from a space of her own: "It''s good
    they are free," she would whisper alone.'
  - And when evening fell and the sun hid away, She trusted her star would return
    from his play. But one day, the new friend, with a fleeting bright flash, Took
    the little one far, turning peace into ash.
  - 'With a sweet glowing path shining bright at the end, He led him to the woods
    like a loyal old friend. But fairy tales hide a dark truth underneath: Beneath
    all that softness were razor-sharp teeth.'
  - The smile turned to a grimace, the toy became prey, And the monster from stars
    showed its hunger that day. When the mother awoke and went out to explore, The
    scene in the woods made her cry to the core.
  - The hug was a trap, choking slowly to death, It shattered his throat, taking
    away his last breath. With blade-like sharp claws it tore the soft chest, The
    mother fell down, a scream stuck in her breast.
  - Like a macabre prize kept without any grace, It gouged out his eyes... bringing
    dark to the place. The games of the beasts have strict rules of pain, And cruel
    was the fate of this love in the rain.
  - Why does the sky punish one who has cried? Leaving a mother completely empty
    inside. Today no one knows the true weight of this end, For a space monster...
    ate her sweet little friend.
  - 
  textoPantalla: {fileID: 238299435}
  audioGrito: {fileID: 1835856900}
  audioGore: {fileID: 1223717293}
  paginaDelSusto: 11
